Divided (595).png|Underwater Breathing
</gallery>
{{Quote|Truly amazing! Limitless cloning capabilities!|[[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]], discovering Ditto's power.<ref name="DWS" />}}
Ditto has the ability to clone himself without limits through binary fission.{{Refn|[[:File:Divided We Stand Pop-up (7).png]]|group = pop-up|name = image}}<ref name="DWS" /> Each Ditto clone is indistinguishable from each other and operates independently, regardless of what the others want them to do. This allows Ditto to do multiple tasks simultaneously or to cover a large area.<ref name="AFoB" />

The extended sensory nodes on Ditto's body{{Refn|Alternate versions of Ditto have sensory nodes in different colors. For example, [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|12-year-old Mutant Kevin]]'s sensory nodes are colored red.<ref>''[[Weapon XI: Part 2]]''</ref>|group = note}} assist in the sensory web that connects all of his clones{{Refn|group = TNP|name = DeviantArt}} by coordinating the hive mind communication between them.{{Refn|[[:File:Ditto's Receptor Nodes.png]]|group = TNP}}{{Refn|group = TNP|name = node}}

Ditto's clones are capable of re-merging back into one. Furthermore, Ditto is able to remotely pull his other clone bodies toward him for this purpose.<ref name="DWS" /> Ditto can stop the duplication process before a clone comes into their independent being, creating half-formed clones with some of their limbs fused and stuck to his own. He used this power once to create a "ladder" of clones, where each "rail" was a continuous chain of fused arms and legs.<ref name="OMWAT">''[[O Mother, Where Art Thou?]]''</ref> Ditto's clones can also dissipate themselves at will, shown when they immediately dissipated themselves before they were attacked by the clones of [[Khyber's Panuncian]].<ref name="AFoB" />

Ditto possesses enhanced durability, demonstrated when he and his clones were still standing after being hit around by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Mutant Lepidopterran-Splixson Hybrid|mutant Lepidopterran/Splixson hybrids]].<ref name="DWS" />

Ditto can jump surprisingly high for his size; while playing basketball, Ditto slam-dunked the ball through a hoop in a way that would be difficult for an average human to jump high enough to do.<ref name="DWS" /> Ditto is also quite agile, as he was able to climb, squeeze, and maneuver his way out of reach of Khyber's Panuncian while being chased.<ref name="AFoB"/>

Ditto can quickly burrow into the ground and breathe underwater.<ref name="AFoB">''[[A Fistful of Brains]]''</ref><ref name="DWS" />

==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow" widths="300">
Divided (465).png|Recharge Mode Inhibition
DittoTogether.png|Forced Combination
UPdC (273).png|Panuncian Predation
Divided (522).png|Electricity Vulnerability
UPdC (185).png|Poor Cold Resistance
Divided (444).png|Shared Pain ('''Original Series''' only)
</gallery>
If Ditto and his clones are too far apart from each other, he cannot change back into [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] until all the duplicates are close enough together. It seems that this requires more power from the Omnitrix than normal, as seen later when he could only transform into [[Upgrade (Classic)|Upgrade]] for a fraction of the normal time limit.<ref name="DWS" />

Ditto's clones can be fused back together with enough force.<ref name="OMWAT" /> 

Being a Splixson, Ditto is at a massive disadvantage against a Panuncian due to them also possessing the ability to clone themselves.<ref>[[Khyber]]</ref><ref name="AFoB" />

Ditto can be harmed by electricity, such as when he was tortured with an electrical prod by [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] while he was held captive in a container filled with water.<ref name="DWS" />

Ditto can be controlled by [[Vladat]]s via their [[Corruptura]]s. However, the latter cannot control all of the Ditto clones as each of them are independent.{{Refn|[[:File:Ditto Clones Independent.PNG]]|group = DJW}} Furthermore, the Corrupturas will not be copied across his clones.{{Refn|[[:File:Ditto Clones and Corrupturas.png]]|group = DJW}}

Ditto is not resistant to extremely cold temperatures.<ref name="AFoB" />

[[File:OMWAT (489).png|right|thumb|192px|Ditto's clones are independent from each other's pain in '''Omniverse''']]
In the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''', Ditto's clones shared a link to keep track of each other,{{Refn|[[:File:Divided We Stand Pop-up (8).png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="DWS" /> making it so that if one Ditto was hurt, all the others would feel the same pain and if one Ditto got killed, the others were automatically killed as well, thus negating the ability to form an army of clones. This is no longer the case as of ''[[O Mother, Where Art Thou?]]'', as each clone is independent from each other's pain, meaning a clone can be killed without harming the others.{{Refn|[[:File:Ditto clones do not share pain in Omniverse.png]]|group = DJW}}{{Refn|[[Contradictory Retcons (Classic)|Contradictory Retcons]]|group = BTP}}

==History==
===Ben 10===
*Ditto first appeared in ''[[Divided We Stand]]'', where he was accidentally unlocked by [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] and fought [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]]'s [[Mutant Seagull|mutant seagull]]. Then, Ditto played basketball with his clones and, eventually, one of the Dittos was caught by Animo to have his DNA copied. Later, Ditto defeated Animo's army of [[Mutant Lepidopterran-Splixson Hybrid|Mutant Lepidopterran/Splixson Hybrid]]s.
*In ''[[Ready to Rumble]]'', Ditto saved [[Mrs. Fang]] and defeated [[Mr. Beck]].

===Five Years Prior to Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', 16-year-old Ben in 11-year-old Ben's body used Ditto to battle [[Eon]] until the latter retreated.

===Alien Force=== 
*Ditto was locked by the Omnitrix's reconfiguration in ''[[Ben 10 Returns: Part 1]]''.

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Ditto was re-unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].

===Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[O Mother, Where Art Thou?]]'', Ditto fought some [[Pretty Boy Clones]] and chased after [[Ma Vreedle]].
*In ''[[A Fistful of Brains]]'', Ditto and his clones tried to escape from [[Panuncian]], but eventually failed in the end.
*In ''[[Animo Crackers]]'', Ditto tried to chase [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Spanner]], but was caught off guard and defeated by [[Dr. Animo (Original Future)|Future Dr. Animo]].
*In ''[[Universe vs. Tennyson]]'', Ditto fought [[Fistrick]], but reverted.
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Ditto appeared for a short time when [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Original Future Timeline|Original Future]]===
*In ''[[Ken 10]]'', [[Ken Tennyson (Original)|Ken]] as Ditto and [[Devlin Levin|Devlin]] found the [[Null Void Projector]].

